I recently found out about a new strategy in #nethack on freenode. I'm not 
sure where it originated, but it's pretty neat. I'm not sure if it's been 
discussed here before; I didn't find anything on it when searching Google 
groups.

Basically, what you do is get a pickaxe and a playable musical instrument as 
soon as possible, then dig straight down to the castle and clear it by 
crushing everything in the drawbridge. If you're successful, you can get the 
castle wand in <5k turns or better. You can get up past xl10 just from 
squashing things, and then you can just grab the wand.

It takes a bit of (real life) luck and liberal use of Elbereth, but it's 
great when it works out. I personally got the castle wand at just over 10k 
turns, which isn't speedy but still let me skip a majority of the dungeon. I 
didn't attempt digging down at all until I had cleared sokoban and did a bit 
of the mines, but it's still very fast. I had to deal with a master lich 
(should have been a lower lvl, I guess) but I had a lucky =oConflict which 
helped a lot.

According to Rodney (info bot in the channel) it works best with elven 
wizards, since elves always start with an instrument, and of course wizards 
can have a lot of useful equipment that helps.

It's pretty fun and exciting, in my opinion... especially when you dig down 
and land next to a monster that ignores Elbereth. Of course, it's a bit 
questionable as far as lameness is concerned (a bit like scumming the 
minetown for a magic lamp, I guess) but it's interesting nonetheless. :P 




